{"t":"Violence Against Women and Girls in Sport","r":"UAN-REPORT-UNSUB-ViolenceAgainstWomen-UNDATED-1","c":"Reports","k":"Submission","d":"Undated","s":"The submission, presented by Kailash Union, examines violence experienced by Hindu women and girls in sport, attributing impacts to what the document characterizes as a \"Hindu holocaust\" and discussing systemic causes rooted in patriarchal norms and historical colonization. The document describes Kailash Union's policies and initiatives addressing women's safety in sports, including zero-tolerance policies against sexual harassment, healthcare provisions, and leadership representation, while also detailing alleged persecution of the Supreme Pontiff of Hinduism and his followers.","u":"reports/uan-report-unsub-violenceagainstwomen-undated-1.html","x":"violence against women and girls in sport the submission, presented by kailash union, examines violence experienced by hindu women and girls in sport, attributing impacts to what the document characterizes as a \"hindu holocaust\" and discussing systemic causes rooted in patriarchal norms and historical colonization. the document describes kailash union's policies and initiatives addressing women's safety in sports, including zero-tolerance policies against sexual harassment, healthcare provisions, and leadership representation, while also detailing alleged persecution of the supreme pontiff of hinduism and his followers. not stated in the document kailash union uan-report-unsub-violenceagainstwomen-undated-1 submission women and girls in sport gender-based violence hindu minority rights kailash union women's empowerment violence against women and girls in sports contexts and systemic barriers to female participation. historical discrimination and alleged persecution of hindu women, including claims of cultural genocide. kailash union's legal status as a sovereign state and its policies on gender equality and women's leadership. alleged persecution of the supreme pontiff of hinduism and kailash union's followers through media campaigns and legal cases. recommendations for international cooperation and the adoption of matrilineal society models to protect female athletes."}
